<% content_for :title, "Support · Gloslate" %>
<% content_for :head do %><meta name="description" content="Get help with Gloslate: signing in, people and groups, payments, and your account."><% end %>
<% content_for :styles do %><style><%= raw File.read(Rails.root.join("app/assets/stylesheets/site.css")) %></style><% end %>
<% support = ENV.fetch("SUPPORT_EMAIL", "support@gloslate.app") %>
<%= render "public/site_nav" %>
<main id="main" class="container">
<article class="doc">
  <div class="eyebrow">Support</div>
  <h1>How can we help?</h1>
  <p class="updated">Most answers are below. If not, email us and a person will reply.</p>

  <div class="card">
    <h2>Contact us</h2>
    <p style="margin:0">Email <a href="mailto:<%= support %>" style="font-weight:800"><%= support %></a>. Include the phone number or email you sign in with (never a sign-in code), and we'll usually reply within two business days.</p>
  </div>

  <h2>Signing in</h2>
  <p><b>My code didn't arrive.</b> Codes come from Gloslate by text or email within a minute. Check your spam folder, make sure the number or email is typed correctly, then tap Send again. Codes expire after 10 minutes.</p>
  <p><b>I changed phone numbers.</b> Sign in another way you've set up, like your email, Apple or Google. If you can't sign in at all, email us and we'll help you get back in.</p>

  <h2>People and groups</h2>
  <p><b>Adding someone.</b> On Home, tap Invite and send them the link. In a group, tap Add someone. You can add people by first name first, and log expenses before they join.</p>
  <p><b>Trips and one-on-one tabs.</b> Open Friends. Start a group for a trip (everyone adds what they paid, and Gloslate finds the fewest payments to settle), or tap Settle up with someone for just one person.</p>
  <p><b>Someone moved out.</b> Settle up first. Bills split by the days each person lived there, and their history stays on your statements.</p>

  <h2>Payments</h2>
  <p><b>A payment is wrong.</b> Open it and tap <i>Something is wrong</i> (or <i>I didn't get this</i> while it's pending). You can do that for 30 days. Gloslate never moves money, so it can't reverse a payment made in Venmo, Cash App or Zelle. For that, contact the payment app.</p>
  <p><b>Someone says they paid.</b> It shows as pending until the person who received it confirms it.</p>

  <h2>Your account</h2>
  <p><b>Export your data:</b> in the app, open You → Your data.</p>

  <h2 id="delete-account">Delete your Gloslate account</h2>
  <p><b>In the app:</b> open the You tab, scroll to the bottom and tap <b>Delete account</b>. It takes effect right away.</p>
  <p><b>Without the app:</b> email <a href="mailto:<%= support %>?subject=Delete%20my%20Gloslate%20account"><%= support %></a> from the email or phone number on your account, with "Delete my Gloslate account" as the subject. I'll confirm it's you and delete it within 30 days.</p>
  <p><b>What's deleted:</b> your name, email, phone number, sign-in methods, profile photo, payment app handles, friends list, notifications, devices and settings.</p>
  <p><b>What stays:</b> expenses and payments you shared with other people stay in their history, labeled "Former member", so their totals stay correct. Nothing in it identifies you. See the <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> for details.</p>
</article>
</main>
<%= render "public/site_footer" %>
